{"kind":"request","text":"Design note and build placement: one environment for the acts of a declared scope, so that a page, an agent and the CLI explore, submit and resolve an act through one body of code.\n\nFiled 2026-11-14 10:12 EST at Hugh's request. Hugh asked for a dated design note in this repository and for its submission to the planner for implementation. Every dap fact in the note is read at main `189cf7b64a`. This request replaces `f70862b3`, which gitseq recorded as ineffective because it named no target.\n\n## Outcome\n\nAn author defines the items and the acts one time. dap then gives each interface six services: describe, observe, explore, compose, submit and resolve. A page, the MCP tools and the CLI give one answer about an act under one stated context. No page writes its own copy of a guard. No page decides how a pending act takes its order, signs again or returns.\n\n## Why\n\nThree partial copies of the judge's admission exist today: `actsOn` in `packages/client/src/forms.ts`, the `when` condition of a view act with the host's repeated checks (`docs/application-views.md`), and the checks that each page writes beside its buttons. The pinboard (`~/play/dap-ui-sdk`) and the shared map (`~/play/dap-foldkit`) each built their own speculation and their own handling of a failure. A review of 13 November 2026 reproduced nine faults in the pinboard. The client note of `e5b86654` (D12) settles one request of one member. It does not explore an unsigned act, hold work that waits for another entry, or serve an agent.\n\n## The note\n\nThe note is `notes/2026-11-14-act-environment.md`, on branch `planner/act-environment-20261114` at commit `e91731d220`, in the worktree `~/play/artroom-worktrees/planner-act-environment-20261114`. A later commit on that branch adds the id of this request to the status line. The note is draft 3, after two reviews. It is not on main, and nothing in it is built.\n\nIts rulings:\n\n1. An act is a plain value: `kind`, `on`, `fields` and the expected revisions. It carries no signature.\n2. Explore judges a complete act with the judge's own code, under a stated context. Its answer is `admitted`, `refused`, `incomplete` or `unavailable`.\n3. The environment gives no step a new basis by itself. Decision A lets a definition declare each subject of an act as `observed` or `current`.\n4. A submit retains an authorization before any signature. One version of one retained authorization permits each signing. This rule replaces D12 rule 3.\n5. A draft keeps the basis that it opened on. This rule changes D12 rule 5.\n6. A dependent act names its source by key and version. A composition is a sequence.\n7. The owner of a step resolves its status from the scope's evidence.\n\n## What the planner does\n\n1. Land the note through review.\n2. Take the seven decisions of section 17 to Hugh for ratification.\n3. Take the three kernel parts of section 16 to Hugh for a ruling under `docs/kernel.md` section 7: the export of the body judgment from `packages/derive`, the explore method on `ScopeApi`, and decision A.\n4. After ratification, file one child request for each build step that the note places: E1 to E6, A and R (section 13).\n\n## Order\n\nThe landing of the note can start now. This request places no build. Steps E1 and E2 need no replica and wait only for their rulings. Step E3 lands with D12 step C4, and step E4 with D12 step C3. Step R is a reservation example on `examples/lending`. It uses existing forms and can start with E1.\n\n## Filing rule\n\nThe note adds no scope kind, no platform definition name, no capability name or form, and no new model of the record. It adds one MCP tool, `explore`, to the tools of a declared scope, and no tool family. An authorization is a record of the client's store, and not a record of a scope. Three parts enter the kernel, and none closes a K item. Decision A also adds one form to the count of K5, and it needs a carrier under section 7.2 of `docs/kernel.md`. Section 16 of the note states each part and its reason. The planner holds each kernel part until Hugh rules.\n\nSource: `~/play/dap-foldkit/ENVIRONMENT.draft-1.md` and `ENVIRONMENT.draft-2.md`, with two reviews of 14 November 2026. Related: D12 `e5b86654`.","body":{"conditions":"The note notes/2026-11-14-act-environment.md lands through review, with its status line. Hugh ratifies the note, or rules on each of the seven decisions of its section 17. Hugh rules on each of the three kernel parts of its section 16 under docs/kernel.md section 7. The planner files one child request for each build step that the ratified note places. No step that adds to the kernel starts before its ruling.","target_head":"189cf7b64a1501b307b9c73e96ee83641c3bd2de","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}